## Current pre-Phase-B state (2026-07-19)

- source follow-up HEAD: `53c996115039cf73bc82d0027871433650994a95`
- notes HEAD: `3c0ce8f9effd7f6a5496200033c0e27dd966839b`
- current `extracted/PIN`: `d5f91f7e88c337b85623d7af6f7cb01cd136f97c`

The notes corpus is still internally consistent with its exact old PIN, but source main has advanced. Before Phase B:

1. decide/freeze the exact source release SHA;
2. repin/extract notes against that SHA;
3. run the source-enabled inspection on the repinned state;
4. run the one-off manual source full-build attestation for the same SHA;
5. only then enable public source checkout and Pages deployment.

No Pages workflow or repository visibility setting was changed in this pass.
